{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/779490-wanting-to-get-into-cwod-where-do-i-start","id":779490,"title":"Wanting to get into cWoD, where do I start?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-03T19:45:35-08:00","id":779490,"title":"Wanting to get into cWoD, where do I start?","content":"I've been hearing about stuff like Vampire: The Masquerade and Werewolf: The Apocalypse for some time now, and recently decided to do some research to see if it was something I wanted to run for my local gaming group. After quite a bit of looking around on various forums and wikis, I've decided that cWoD sounds like a better fit for my group than nWoD. The question I have now is, where do I start? I'd like to know which game line is the best for newcomers to the storyteller system, the sourcebooks that I'd need to run it, and which books to pick up to best start the metaplot. Any other general tips you have for World of Darkness newbies would also be helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10038-superguin200","name":"superguin200","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10038_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T20:02:13-08:00","id":779502,"title":"","content":"Well there is no &quot;main&quot; book for the setting like nwod, so really it's pick up a game and go. I would advise that you avoid cross overs to begin with if at all, but that's my bias. <br /> <br /> The 20th anniversary books are a good start point but if you don't want to spend that much coin pick up a revised book, and maybe the storytelling and players guides too. The screens help a bit also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T20:12:23-08:00","id":779505,"title":"","content":"Well, there's a very useful &quot;book&quot; in the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/89815/Dark-Ages-Basic-Rules\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Ages Basic Rules</a>. It's not going to help much with the setting, and the metaplot side of things, but it's a nice read for what the essential cWOD rules look like (as best as you can given the number of variations there are). It's a Revised era document, so it will be different from the newer 20th anniversary books, but it's enough to get a better idea of the basics.<br /> <br /> Otherwise nothing more to add than Dwight's points. You're going to want to settle on one of the game lines (Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage are the easiest right now since the 20th books, while massive slogs, cover a lot of things that are spread around multiple books previously) to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T21:21:19-08:00","id":779528,"title":"","content":"If you like political intrigue and centuries-old antagonists, then Vampire is your best bet.<br /> <br /> If you like fighting against Lovecraftian entities who literally control aspects of reality, then check out Werewolf.<br /> <br /> If you like philosophical and social themes including discussions about potential vs safety, then Mage will serve you well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T01:17:56-08:00","id":779612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/779490-wanting-to-get-into-cwod-where-do-i-start?p=779528#post779528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you like political intrigue and centuries-old antagonists, then Vampire is your best bet.<br /> <br /> If you like fighting against Lovecraftian entities who literally control aspects of reality, then check out Werewolf.<br /> <br /> If you like philosophical and social themes including discussions about potential vs safety, then Mage will serve you well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, there is actually a fair amount of political intrigue in Werewolf if you're playing sept to sept and higher levels of organization. Secondly, an awful lot of what Garou and Fera struggle against isn't actually Lovecraftian. Its ultimate source kind of is if you squint, but there's an awful lot of familiar worldly ills that go into the struggle, as well as the question of how to address them. A substitute simple pitch would be &quot;if you care to examine visceral outrage at the state of the world versus the calmer demeanor needed to actually solve problems&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T02:29:12-08:00","id":779635,"title":"","content":"Yes, there's a lot of crossover thematically. I was simplifying for the sake of accessibility. When you think political intrigue in cWoD you don't think Werewolf, despite the inter-sept issues, you think Vampire. You think fighting against Lovecraftian beings you don't think Mage, you think Werewolf. It <i>happens</i>, but it doesn't occupy the central role like it does in the named game lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T04:01:19-08:00","id":779679,"title":"","content":"If you want a game where literally nothing matters in the long run, and everything will be destroyed by pseudolovecraftian beings, or a game about searching for hope where it might not exist, you want Wraith.<br /> <br /> If you want a game where science is silly and wrong because it destroys wonder and creativity, then you need a different person to write the pitch for Changeling because I think it will only become a good game if the C20 core is more respectful of the wonder from understanding.<br /> <br /> If you want a game about a bunch of hypocrites desperately fighting supernatural creatures to free them from humanity and having trouble succeeding, you want Hunter. Hypocrisy can be lessened if you want, especially as their powers might be borrowed.<br /> <br /> If you want a game about trying to fit into a society you barely understand, both more and less advanced than you're used to, with a passtime of trying to make sure both the crazy and the 'a god am I' members of your species, look into Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T06:45:53-08:00","id":779763,"title":"","content":"For introducing new players, I definitely recommend Hunter the Reckoning first. It is the easiest to just kind of dive into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T08:11:35-08:00","id":779822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/779490-wanting-to-get-into-cwod-where-do-i-start?p=779635#post779635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, there's a lot of crossover thematically. I was simplifying for the sake of accessibility. When you think political intrigue in cWoD you don't think Werewolf, despite the inter-sept issues, you think Vampire. You think fighting against Lovecraftian beings you don't think Mage, you think Werewolf. It <i>happens</i>, but it doesn't occupy the central role like it does in the named game lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I do think Mage when I consider fighting against Lovecraftian beings, because I prefer to keep HP far away from Werewolf and reference other touchpoints for its animistic world. Mage, however, is a crazy Frankenstein's Monster, so sure, throw them in. You threw <i>everything else</i> in, so why stop there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T08:31:24-08:00","id":779835,"title":"","content":"Okay, from what you've all said I think Vampire: The Masquerade sounds the most appealing. I'll download the Dark Ages rulebook at Heavy Arms' suggestion, then go to the 20th Anniversary book from there. Now I'd like to know where to start with the metaplot, and if using revised edition sourcebooks with the 20th anniversary ruleset will cause any major problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10038-superguin200","name":"superguin200","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10038_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T08:48:42-08:00","id":779844,"title":"","content":"There really isn't a &quot;meta plot&quot; sourcebook, certain events that happen but really it's up to you to if you want to use them or run the game during them.<br /> <br /> However I would suggest getting one of the &quot;location&quot;by night books, Chicago is my favorite. They contain a setting, nps and plots for you to run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T09:10:59-08:00","id":779863,"title":"","content":"The best thing for metaplot guidance is to pick a city and get that city's by night sourcebook, as it will have most of the relevant metaplot up to the point it was published.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T10:32:33-08:00","id":779932,"title":"","content":"I'd avoid the metaplot if you're new to oWoD and then research it more after you've played a game or two to see if you like the metaplot. Not everyone is into the metaplot, but some people are. It really is all a matter of taste and what your ST is intending for their chronicle. The best place to start thematically would be the 1e corebook, but that is rare and the rules are wonky, so I'd say go with Vampire: The Masquerade 20th Anniversary Edition or V20 for short. It's the most complete of all the books, is metaplot-neutral (doesn't force the metaplot onto you but does have options for if you want to use the metaplot), and is the most mechanically superior of the Masquerade corebooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T12:54:48-08:00","id":780066,"title":"","content":"It sounds like you're looking at the metaplot as a source of adventure hooks - which it can be, but they're often embedded in books across the various lines. There are timeline guides for the various games that flag what happens when and where it appears. (The forthcoming <b>Beckett's Jyhad Diary</b> is a <b>Vampire: The Masquerade 20th Anniversary Edition</b> sourcebook about metaplot events and various ways to use them, while the rest of the <b>V20</b> line largely avoids metaplot and references the changes it made to the setting over the years in sidebars.)<br /> <br /> If you're looking for ready-to-use adventures and chronicles, they're available as standalone books and as part of sourcebooks, and there's a list <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/402431-ready-to-play-adventures\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-04T13:12:25-08:00","id":780082,"title":"","content":"If you're into metaplot, pick up:<br /> <br /> Nights of Prophecy<br /> Time of Thin Blood<br /> The 'by Night' books<br /> The clanbook series<br /> <br /> The first book has plenty of story ideas. The second details a lot of the Final Nights stuff. The 'by Night' books detail cities and often have much smaller metaplot developments, providing for plot hooks without causing huge setting changes. The clanbooks offer lots of clan secrets (and delusions) that shed light on the history of Cainites (or obfuscate it).<br /> <br /> The Giovanni Chronicles and Transylvanian Chronicles have sweeping chronicle ideas that feed into the wider metaplot quite heavily.<br /> <br /> But if you buy Vampire Revised, I only think you need the core book plus Guide to the Camarilla and Guide to the Sabbat. The ST's Companion and ST's Handbook are useful too. Everything else is just fluff (okay, not quite, but only the first three books are really 'essential' in my mind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T06:41:51-08:00","id":780537,"title":"","content":"I'd ignore the meta-plot as well. Pick a place and if there is no by Night book design it. I generally use my hometown I know parts of it very well and it is a bit of fun to darken the area. For npcs I generally use people I know for example the Prince is my High School Gym teacher, a friend's Dad is the chief harpy, the primogen are an assortment of old bosses.<br /> <br /> If you are using a by Night book I'd probably avoid Montreal and Berlin .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T12:29:35-08:00","id":780659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/779490-wanting-to-get-into-cwod-where-do-i-start?p=780537#post780537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd ignore the meta-plot as well. Pick a place and if there is no by Night book design it. I generally use my hometown I know parts of it very well and it is a bit of fun to darken the area. For npcs I generally use people I know for example the Prince is my High School Gym teacher, a friend's Dad is the chief harpy, the primogen are an assortment of old bosses.<br /> <br /> If you are using a by Night book I'd probably avoid Montreal and Berlin .</div> </div> </div> </div>Montreal is actually decent for Sabbat players, showing how the Sabbat actually runs their cities, although it is a bit crass. I agree with you on Berlin, that one is awful. Chicago By Night 1e is the best of the &quot;by Night&quot; books in my opinion though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T16:53:36-08:00","id":780784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/779490-wanting-to-get-into-cwod-where-do-i-start?p=779822#post779822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I do think Mage when I consider fighting against Lovecraftian beings, because I prefer to keep HP far away from Werewolf and reference other touchpoints for its animistic world. Mage, however, is a crazy Frankenstein's Monster, so sure, throw them in. You threw <i>everything else</i> in, so why stop there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hear, hear. Although there are some things in the Mythos that resonate with Werewolf, Mythos as a style of antagonist suits better to Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T16:55:13-08:00","id":780786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>superguin200</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/779490-wanting-to-get-into-cwod-where-do-i-start?p=779835#post779835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, from what you've all said I think Vampire: The Masquerade sounds the most appealing. I'll download the Dark Ages rulebook at Heavy Arms' suggestion, then go to the 20th Anniversary book from there. Now I'd like to know where to start with the metaplot, and if using revised edition sourcebooks with the 20th anniversary ruleset will cause any major problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't start with the metaplot. It's directly tied to apocalyptic events and characters that are completley irrelevant almost 25 years later. Take the 20th Anniversary, and make it your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-12T18:05:34-08:00","id":785091,"title":"","content":"It really depends on the game you want to run<br /> <br /> Want to explore the dehumanizing effects of immortality and predation on humans with a splash of action and political intrigue, vampire is the way to go.<br /> <br /> Want to play a rage monster shapeshifter (I've never played but always used it's source books) then werewolf is for you. <br /> <br /> I've never played mage, couldn't find a group for it.<br /> <br /> Want to explore being an ancient spirit that helped build creation and now is confined to a mortal host, dealing with having human memories, wants, and desires. Add in the same splash of action and political intrigue as vampire and you have demon the fallen, which is my favorite CWoD game<br /> <br /> I've never played changeling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}